Clearing a ready thread's units, by a revoke or by the destroy of its pool, leaves it on its queue and its account as it was.
Its next turn would run a thread that may not run, or memory that is no longer a thread;
the queues hold only live threads that may run, and no account holds more than its units hold.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place names a queue it is not for
Report: a place's account holds more than its cap

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -534,7 +534,7 @@ void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
     }
     *bound = (struct cap){ 0 };
     /* An empty place holds nothing, so settling empties its account as it takes the place off its queue. */
-    lender_settle(t);
+    (void)t;
